cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mera.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mera.jl: geometrically exact, reproducible analysis of RAMSES simulations in Julia"
abstract: >-
  Mera.jl is an analysis framework for astrophysical simulations, written in Julia. It covers the
  whole path from raw simulation output to a result you can publish: selecting regions, computing
  physics in any unit, projecting from any viewing angle, profiles, phase diagrams, clump finding,
  time series and movies. It reads RAMSES adaptive mesh refinement output natively, with hydro and
  MHD, particles, gravity, clumps, sinks and radiative transfer, and handles cosmological runs
  throughout. A snapshot is one table, one row per cell with its refinement level, so nothing is
  flattened onto a uniform grid first. When a selected region cuts through a cell, Mera counts the
  part of the cell that lies inside, and a map holds the same mass at any angle, pixel size or
  thread count. Mera also renders volumes, finds clumps with seven algorithms, and rewrites a RAMSES
  output so it restarts on any number of CPUs. Every file it saves records the snapshot, the code
  and the package versions behind it, and one call bundles these records into an RO-Crate. Readers
  plug into a registry, so a reader written in another package works with the whole analysis.
  This development line also reads AREPO, GADGET, PLUTO, Athena++, FLASH, Chombo and AMReX/Quokka
  through the same registry and the same analysis layer, unchanged. The AMReX/Quokka reader was
  contributed by ChongChong He.
type: software
